// Pull request author: mikedsosa
// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: ADExplorer Writing Complete AD Snapshot Into .dat File
// Sigma ID: 0a1255c5-d732-4b62-ac02-b5152d34fb83
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Arnim Rupp (Nextron Systems), Thomas Patzke
// Date: 2025-07-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1087.002, T1069.002, T1482
// Description: Detects the dual use tool ADExplorer writing a complete AD snapshot into a .dat file. This can
//   be used by attackers to extract data for Bloodhound, usernames for password spraying or use the
//   meta data for social engineering. The snapshot doesn't contain password hashes but there have
//   been cases, where administrators put passwords in the comment field.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of ADExplorer by administrators creating .dat snapshots
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/adexplorer
//   - https://github.com/c3c/ADExplorerSnapshot.py/tree/f700904defac330802bbfedd1d8ffd9248f4ee24
//   - https://www.packetlabs.net/posts/scattered-spider-is-a-young-ransomware-gang-exploiting-large-corporations/
//   - https://www.nccgroup.com/us/research-blog/lapsus-recent-techniques-tactics-and-procedures/
//   - https://trustedsec.com/blog/adexplorer-on-engagements
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/2de0cded073187dfb8bda849b7f69f79e5d1d473/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_sysinternals_adexplorer_dump_written.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ADExp.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ADExplorer.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ADExplorer64.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ADExplorer64a.exe") and FolderPath endswith ".dat"
